,"site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":112,"digest":"sha256:4121799d2f9df2712501ac652e715793257256dae7bc3fe79b6980079ac26923","download_count":4,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z"},{"id":659195781,"node_id":"RA_kwDORj5l3c4nSoeF","name":"h5i-websec-v0.5.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/gzip","state":"uploaded","size":3236585,"digest":"sha256:7fed4fed1ddce572a9ba66a1718f855c492c144942dfa7b17954e2e44d1372ca","download_count":10,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z"},{"id":659195802,"node_id":"RA_kwDORj5l3c4nSoea","name":"h5i-websec-v0.5.1-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz.sha256","label":"","uploader":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/octet-stream","state":"uploaded","size":117,"digest":"sha256:58e00bad5fd4f3755b6bd7c3e7bb9502902df1e3d7ed0bd6edaf98b1e8018d70","download_count":9,"created_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T11:53:50Z"}],"body":"## Install\n\nOne binary. `h5i` unifies web development, formal verification\nwith Lean 4, and red-teaming around a composable Rust framework.\n\n**Linux / macOS:**\n```bash\ncurl -L https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/releases/download/v0.5.1/h5i-v0.5.1-<TARGET>.tar.gz | tar -xz\nsudo mv h5i /usr/local/bin/\n```\n\n**Windows:** download the `.zip`, extract `h5i.exe`, and add it to your `PATH`.\n\n### The browser\n\n```bash\nh5i browser open https://example.com\nh5i browser snapshot\nh5i browser requests     # what it asked for, and what was refused\nh5i browser audit        # the whole session, afterwards\n```\n\nA session is Chromium, driven through\n[agent-browser](https://github.com/vercel-labs/agent-browser)\n(`npm install -g agent-browser`), and captured at a proxy this\nbinary runs: every request is policy-checked and written down\nbefore it moves.\n\n### The websec workbench\n\n`h5i-websec` is a separate archive, and installing it is a\ndeliberate act:\n\n```bash\ncurl -L https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/releases/download/v0.5.1/h5i-websec-v0.5.1-<TARGET>.tar.gz | tar -xz\nh5i plugin install websec --from ./h5i-websec\n```\n\nIt holds no privilege of its own: every verb runs the `h5i browser`\nverbs a person would type, through the same policy, budget and\nreceipts.\n\n### The recon ledger\n\n`h5i-recon` is the other plugin, and it arrives the same way:\n\n```bash\ncurl -L https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/releases/download/v0.5.1/h5i-recon-v0.5.1-<TARGET>.tar.gz | tar -xz\nh5i plugin install recon --from ./h5i-recon\n```\n\nIt records what a target exposes, where each candidate came from,\nand which stored message confirmed it. Discovery only: a URL read\nout of a bundle stays a candidate until a request answers for it,\nand nothing here is called a vulnerability.\n\n### Security regression tests\n\n`h5i-test` replays repository-owned attack flows and hands their\nevidence to repository-owned external oracles:\n\n```bash\ncurl -L https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/releases/download/v0.5.1/h5i-test-v0.5.1-<TARGET>.tar.gz | tar -xz\nh5i plugin install test --from ./h5i-test\nh5i test .h5i-tests/tests --target http://localhost:3000\n```\n\nIt writes JSON and JUnit. OpenAPI coverage is report-only unless\n`--min-coverage` is explicitly supplied.\n\nEvery request it makes is checked against an allowlist — every\nrequest and every redirect hop — and written to the log before any\nbytes move. A request that is not in `h5i browser requests` did not\nhappen. What a box adds, with `--in`, is that the record gains a\nwitness outside the browser; on a bare host that part is not\nclaimed.\n\n### Available targets\n\n| Target | Platform |\n|--------|---------|\n| `x86_64-unknown-linux-musl` | Linux x86_64 (static, glibc-free) |\n| `aarch64-unknown-linux-musl` | Linux arm64 (static, glibc-free) |\n| `aarch64-apple-darwin` | macOS Apple Silicon (arm64) |\n| `x86_64-pc-windows-msvc` | Windows x86_64 |\n\nIntel Macs have no published build: Rosetta 2 translates x86_64 to\narm64, not the reverse, so the `aarch64-apple-darwin` archive will\nnot run there. Build from source instead:\n`cargo install --git https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i`\n\nEach archive is accompanied by a `.sha256` checksum file.\n\n\n## What's Changed\n* Add svg by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/708\n* Koukyosyumei patch 1 by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/707\n* Koukyosyumei patch 1 by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/709\n* Revise README to streamline application logic description by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/710\n* Simplify HTTP security testing description by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/711\n* install.sh: fall back to a user directory when sudo refuses by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/712\n* install.sh: install into ~/.local/bin by default, without sudo by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/713\n* restyle calculator proof svg to match h5i ui by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/714\n* Improve style by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/716\n* improve slides by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/717\n* Update README with UI section and reordering by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/718\n* Rename 'UI' section to 'Dashboard' by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/719\n* Improve svg by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/720\n* Eliminate duplicate h5i compatibility statement by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/721\n* improve svg by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/722\n* Koukyosyumei patch 1 by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/723\n* add animation by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/724\n* h5i-app-std: add a proven HashMap without new axioms by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/715\n* App engine perf by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/725\n* docs/app: point Conduit links to h5i-app-bench; fix the reads test pa… by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/726\n* docs: browser proxy covers sites the engine cannot read by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/727\n* Change project title in README.md by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/728\n* browser: decode zstd, store proxy-observed bodies decoded, replay wit… by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/729\n* Websec zstd by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/731\n* skill/websec: document the blind-oracle workflow by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/732\n* App gpu by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/730\n* Generalize GPU backend inputs and validate batch outputs by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/733\n* Koukyosyumei patch 1 by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/734\n* Update README.md by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/735\n* Update README.md by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/736\n* Revise installation instructions in README.md by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/737\n* Update section title from 'Test' to 'Hack' by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/739\n* Optimize read subqueries by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/738\n* Improve doc update by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/740\n* Websec match all and error ux by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/741\n* Improve demo flow around one board app by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/742\n* Improve front by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/743\n* remove our own browser, and focus on using proxy-mode by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/744\n* websec/browser: nudge toward `--as` when a replay goes out unauthenti… by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/745\n* bump h5i to v0.5.1 and h5i-app to 0.1.2 by @Koukyosyumei in https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/pull/748\n\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/h5i-dev/h5i/compare/v0.5.0...v0.5.1","mentions_count":1}
